---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Concrete Demo | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="concrete" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/concrete-preview.webp" alt="Concrete contractor demo preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">Concrete Contractor Demo</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A fictional local contractor landing page for a concrete services business, designed to show how a traditional service company can communicate trust, explain services, and generate quote requests.</p>
      <a href="https://concrete.carlosmenco.site/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View demo <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>This project is a fictional demo for a concrete contractor in Fort Collins. It uses a local-service website structure: clear positioning, service categories, trust-building sections, FAQs, and a guided quote request flow.</p>
      <p>The goal was to create a realistic business website that feels usable for residential and commercial services without needing a real client brief.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Demo concept, landing page structure, service content organization, conversion flow planning, visual direction, responsive implementation, and portfolio presentation.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>Local contractor websites need to build trust quickly. Visitors want to know what services are available, whether the company feels reliable, and how easy it is to request a quote before they commit to a call.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Structured the page around concrete services, quality signals, local trust, FAQs, and a quote path.</li>
        <li>Used direct, service-focused messaging for patios, driveways, stamped concrete, commercial concrete, and curbing.</li>
        <li>Created a guided quote flow that asks for project type, location, timeline, and contact details.</li>
        <li>Kept the demo realistic enough to work as a starter direction for a future local service website.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The demo works as a practical example of a high-intent service landing page: clear, local, conversion-focused, and easy to adapt for a real contractor or home-services business.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
